# Implementation Plan - Task 9.2: Monitoring & Error Tracking Setup

This implementation plan details the setup and configuration of Sentry, Vercel Analytics, error boundaries, performance tracking, alert definitions, and database monitoring queries for the AI-Assured Compliance Dashboard.

## Status Quo
* **Error Tracking**: Application-wide errors and API failures are logged locally to standard output/console, but there is no centralized telemetry tool to capture, aggregate, and alert on production failures.
* **UI Resilience**: No centralized error boundary components exist; client-side rendering crashes fall back to browser defaults.
* **Performance Telemetry**: No response latency tracing, p95 monitoring, or user analytics are configured.
* **Database Checks**: No reference scripts exist for querying PostgreSQL metrics (e.g. connection pool saturation, slow queries, index stats).

---

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> Sentry and Vercel Analytics integrations require project DSN keys. For this setup:
> * Sentry will utilize the `SENTRY_DSN` and `NEXT_PUBLIC_SENTRY_DSN` environment variables.
> * Vercel Analytics will resolve automatically when deployed to Vercel, or via standard environment variables.
> * Alert thresholds (Error Rate > 1%, p95 > 1s) must be manually configured in Sentry's dashboard based on the documentation provided in `docs/monitoring.md`.

---

